Wetin fit cause dis kain problem? Which kind test dem fit do for di pikin? Wetin be di emergency steps wey health workers suppose take immediately? And which kind treatment dem fit give dis newborn pikin?", "answer": "Dis pikin get birth asphyxia or neonatal encephalopathy wey fit cause by prolonged labour, cord prolapse, or placenta problem wey cut oxygen give pikin. Immediate step na to call for help, dry pikin well, clear airway, and start bag-mask ventilation within one minute if pikin no dey cry or breathe well. Check heart rate, if e dey less than 100, continue ventilation and prepare for chest compression and adrenaline if needed. Admit pikin for SCN care: monitor vitals, blood sugar, seizures, give IV fluids, antibiotics if infection suspected, and therapeutic cooling if available and criteria meet. Mama need counseling and support for breastfeeding expression while pikin stabilize.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "5", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "5", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "1", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "5"}

{"question": "we see one of our pregnant unwere early this morning with her husband she talk say she di get serious pain for belle and her bag dey pain her too even though e never reach the time wey dey expect mean she born behind some many months belle she don reach and she talk see na six months and some days she still also whether deepen dey continue or e dey command go and she talk say dey pin dey dear continuously because whether she don see water or blood and she say she don see boat water i'm glad be still ask whether na first back na signs she say yes na first ballet i'm question be dis she if e be say all dis signs na sign of labor wey start before time or if e be say di pregnancy dey miss carry or na another problem if e advise di sumami she go scan imi did leath no we send e happen", "answer": "Based on wetin you describe, dis fit be **preterm labour** (labour wey start before time), because di woman don reach six months (28 weeks) and she dey get continuous belle pain wey no dey stop, plus her water don break (di boat water she talk about na di amniotic fluid wey comot). Since di pregnancy don pass 28 weeks, e no be miscarriage again — na preterm labour or **PPROM** (premature rupture of membrane) we dey talk about, because miscarriage na when pregnancy loss happen before 28 weeks.

Di fact say she don see water wey comot mean say her membrane don rupture, so you must to check am well-well and reduce vaginal examination to prevent infection. **Refer am quick-quick** go hospital wey get facility for premature baby (NICU), and if e possible, give **antenatal steroids (dexamethasone)** to help di baby lungs mature, plus **antibiotics** to prevent infection.

Make you scan am to confirm how di baby dey, check di fluid level and di baby heartbeat, but no let scan delay di referral or treatment because time dey important for dis kain case.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "5", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "5", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "1", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "5"}

{"question": "I be woman wey dey 32 years I born my pikin just 7 days ago Since then I notice say anytime I wan breastfeed am e dey struggle to suck di breast E fit suck small come remove him mouth If I put di breast back for him mouth e go suck small again con move As I dey wonder why e no dey suck breast well I notice say Today the pikin get catarrh E no dey breathe well Anytime e dey breathe e sound like person wey nose block or person stone I call my mother in law come see am She talk say maybe as I born the pikin or tire enter him head or something like that But I dey think say if anything like that happen the nosis and doctors wey help me deliver di baby for now Wetin dey pain me pass be say di pikin no dey feed well E dey make me worry and my mind no dey rest E no dey suck breast well and by 1st I dey try make e breastfeed Most times I go even wake am from sleep before e go suck breast small And sometimes e no go gree sef Abeg wetin fit dey cause this scatarrh wey dey make my pikin no dey breathe well and why e dey sound like person wey nose block every time e dey breathe Wetin fit also be the reason why e no dey suck breast well", "answer": "Mama, no worry too much, wetin dey happen fit be simple thing. Newborn pikin dey breathe through him nose, so if catarrh block di nose, e go hard for am to breathe well and suck breast at di same time, because when e wan suck, e go close him mouth and use nose breathe. Di "nose block" sound and struggle to suck na sign say mucus block di small nostrils.

Wetin you fit do: use warm water make di house moist, and use saline drops (salt water wey dem sell for chemist for baby nose) put small for each nostril, den use bulb syringe gently comot di mucus before you feed am. Clean di nose small before every feed and hold am upright small when e dey suck.

But make you carry di pikin go hospital sharp-sharp if you see any of dis: e no dey suck at all, e dey breathe fast well-well, e dey pull chest inside when e breathe, e dey turn blue or him lips dey dark, e get fever or e too weak. For 7-day-old pikin, breathing wahala fit turn serious quick-quick, so no waste time make nurse or doctor check am make dem confirm say na ordinary catarrh and no be infection.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "5", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "5", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "1", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "5"}

{"question": "I notice say my small sister wey been de laugh happy before and wey been de play with him friends come change just like that Now she dey stay alone for inside her room every day She don remove herself comot from talk wey people dey talk and the things wey she been dey like to do before she no come like them again I also notice say even for house she no dey wan chop with us She dey look as if she no happy or like person wey dey tire every time Wetin fit dey cause her to just start avoid her friends like that E fit be sadness wahala abi things wey dey disturb her for mind abi na fear fear How e fit help her so that she go happy again Which warning signs make we dey look out for Make she see counsellor abi mental health professional", "answer": "Wetin dey happen to your sister fit be **depression** (wey we dey call sadness sickness) or anxiety wahala, especially as she don comot herself from friends, no dey wan chop, dey tire, and no dey enjoy things wey she like before—these na strong signs of depression. E fit come from things wlike stress, bullying, wahala for school, hormone change if she dey grow, or something bad wey happen to her wey she never talk.

To help am, make you and family show am love, talk to am gently without vexing, listen well make she fit open up, and no force am but let am know say una dey there for am. **The serious warning signs wey una MUST watch** na if she talk say she wan die or she no wan live again, if she dey harm her body, dey give her things comot, or no dey sleep and eat at all—if any of these show, carry am go hospital sharp sharp.

Yes o, e very good make she see counsellor or mental health professional (like psychologist or psychiatrist) because dem fit find out wetin dey worry am and treat am with talk therapy or medicine if e serious. No delay—the quick una take act, na so she go fit recover well and happy again.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "5", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "5", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "1", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "5"}

