{"question": "One woman wey dey 30 years old don born pikin few minutes wey don pass. Dem talk say di delivery go normal. But since Dem born di pikin, di pikin dey get serious problem. Di pikin no dey cry well and e no dey respond like new baby suppose respond. After birth, di pikin no cry well at all and e be like say e dey find am hard to wake up. Di pikin body fit dey stiff or e no dey move well as dem expect. Di pikin no fit suck breast well and e dey struggle to breastfeed.

Di mama dey worry because all her other pikin dem cry immediately after dem born dem.

Wetin fit cause dis kain problem? Which kind test dem fit do for di pikin? Wetin be di emergency steps wey health workers suppose take immediately? And which kind treatment dem fit give dis newborn pikin?", "answer": "Newborn peikin dey cry a lot, dey cry like newborn baby, dey cry a lot, dey cry a lot, dey cry a lot.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "1", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "1", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "1", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "1"}

{"question": "Mama wey born pikin two weeks ago begin dey see small-small blood dey come from her body. As days dey pass, e notice say wetin resemble meat or tissue and blood dey come out. Sometimes e dey feel somehow, and e neck no dey okay. E still dey get small-small pain for under belle, and anytime e see all these signs, e dey fear and confuse. E begin wonder wetin dey happen,whether na normal thing wey fit happen after woman born pikin or whether na another sickness.

One day, as e go hospital and dey talk with other nursing mothers, e hear say make nobody ignore any change wey dem notice for their body after childbirth. That one make am decide say e go see doctor make dem examine am.

My question be: Wetin fit cause this kind problem after woman don born? Pain for under belle fit be signs of sickness? Which danger signs wey new mama suppose watch out for after childbirth? And wetin be the steps wey new mama need to take to prevent this kind sickness?", "answer": "Dis one fit be retained products of conception or postpartum hemorrhage wey fit cause infection like endometritis. Di tissue and blood wey you dey see mean say placenta or membrane fit remain for womb, and di lower abdominal pain with foul smell na sign of infection. New mama suppose watch out for heavy bleeding, fever, bad smelling discharge, and severe belle pain as danger signs. Make you run go hospital quick for examination, ultrasound, and possible evacuation (MVA) plus antibiotics. To prevent am, ensure complete placenta delivery, good hygiene, early breastfeeding, and attend postnatal clinic for checkup.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "5", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "5", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "1", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "5"}

{"question": "Good evening. I come because of my younger sibling. I notice say hin eye and skin don begin turn yellow. This thing don dey happen for three days now. Hin body too dey very hot, fever dey worry am, and e no fit chop anything. Anything wey hin chop no dey stay hin belle. E dey vomit everything. As if that one no reach, e dey shake well well because hin head dey pain am and hin whole body dey burn with fever.

We don try give am some medicine for house, but nothing don change. That yellow color for hin eye and skin no gree stop, instead e dey increase everyday. E no dey comfortable at all, e dey really suffer. God forbid, e dey suffer too much. Na why I come hospital make una help us know wetin dey happen and wetin we suppose do. So that my younger sibling go recover and the yellow color for hin skin and eye disappear
", "answer": "I sorry to hear about your brother's condition. The yellow colour for him eye and skin, together with fever, vomiting, and pain, strongly suggests him get jaundice, which fit be a sign of a serious liver problem like hepatitis or malaria. Since his condition dey get three days and e no dey get better, e fit be a severe infection or liver failure. You must rush am for a doctor to see, for serious test, and for proper treatment, because e fit be life-threatening. E important make him get hospital care fast for e to get the right medication and for avoid any danger.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "5", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "5", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "1", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "5"}

{"question": "Mama wey born pikin two weeks ago begin dey see small-small blood dey come from her body. As days dey pass, e notice say wetin resemble meat or tissue and blood dey come out. Sometimes e dey feel somehow, and e neck no dey okay. E still dey get small-small pain for under belle, and anytime e see all these signs, e dey fear and confuse. E begin wonder wetin dey happen,whether na normal thing wey fit happen after woman born pikin or whether na another sickness.

One day, as e go hospital and dey talk with other nursing mothers, e hear say make nobody ignore any change wey dem notice for their body after childbirth. That one make am decide say e go see doctor make dem examine am.

My question be: Wetin fit cause this kind problem after woman don born? Pain for under belle fit be signs of sickness? Which danger signs wey new mama suppose watch out for after childbirth? And wetin be the steps wey new mama need to take to prevent this kind sickness?", "answer": "Mama, the thing wey she dey experience, especially that meat and blood wey dey come out, fit be signs of heavy bleeding or infection after birth, which na serious matter. The pain for under belly and her neck no dey well fit show say infection don start to spread for her body, which we dey call postpartum infection. New mama suppose watch out for high fever, bad smell for the discharge, or heavy bleeding wey no dey stop, because these na "red flags." To prevent this, she must keep her wound clean, drink plenty water, and go see doctor sharp-sharp if any pain dey increase. Since she don go hospital, the doctor go check if she need antibiotics or treatment to clear the infection fast.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "3", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "2", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "2", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "2"}

{"question": "One mama wey dey always bring her pikin come for injection talk say she don notice say her newborn baby get problem for mouth area, and the baby lips dey look blue.

Today too, she notice say anytime she dey breastfeed the baby, the baby dey struggle, dey gasp for air, and e dey find am hard to breathe well. She say na this one make her worry because she no know wetin dey happen to the baby.

Wetin fit make newborn baby lips dey look blue? Wetin fit make baby dey struggle and find am hard to breathe anytime e dey suck breast? Medicine fit solve the problem, abi the baby need make doctor examine am first?", "answer": "O, o, o, o, o. Di baby leyi get problem called cyanosis. Lip leyi dey blue, so baby leyi no get enough oxygen. Baby leyi struggle, gasp, and hard to breathe when breast-feeding. Medicine no solve problem, so baby leyi need see doctor first. Doctor fit diagnose problem and give proper treatment. Di problem leyi fit be respiratory or heart problem. Doctor fit help baby leyi get better.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "5", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "5", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "1", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "5"}

{"question": "One woman wey get belle for six months we dey stay our house begin notice say hin heart dey beat fast fast like person wey just finish race. Sometimes e go just just Dey tire even though e never do any work and hin hand dey shake small small.
After some weeks, e come notice say front of hin neck begin swell. As people begin tell am say hin neck no be like before again, fear catch am. E begin wonder whether Na one of the sickness wey dey affect women wey get belle or whether Na another problem entirely.

Now e don decide say e wan go see doctor make dem check wetin dey cause am. My question be say wetin fit make pregnant woman heart dey beat fast like person wey just run finish, with neck swelling? This problem fit affect the growth and development of the pikin wey dey hin belle? Wetin be the danger signs wey dey suppose watch out for while dem dey house? And e get any type of food and drink wey dem suppose avoid, or any wey e suppose chop and drink during this kind time?", "answer": "Dis symptoms fit be hyperthyroidism (overactive thyroid) wey fit start or worsen for pregnancy, especially Graves disease. E fit affect pikin growth, cause premature birth, low birth weight, or thyroid problem for pikin if no treat am well. Danger signs na: heart dey beat pass 110-120 per minute for rest, serious shortness of breath, chest pain, high fever, severe vomiting, or if swelling for neck dey block breathing or swallowing. Make she avoid plenty iodine things like kelp supplements or excess iodized salt, but normal food with iodine dey okay; make she chop balanced diet with protein, vegetables, and fruits. She must see doctor quick quick for thyroid function test (TSH, Free T4) and possible treatment with safe medicine like propylthiouracil for first trimester.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "4", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "4", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "1", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "5"}

{"question": "one woman noticed say for the past few days pikin don dey coat without stopping at first she tink say na ordinary cold wey catch the pikin for chest and say e go clear by itself but the cough no gree stop every night the pikin dey wake up suddenly because of the cough sometimes e go dey struggle like say e add am to breathway the woman go carry the pikin upright and she free hear the chest they make sound and they work out as the pikin dey breath because of dis the pikin no fit sleep well for night one day after one night read the pikin cough well well and yu struggle to breath properly the woman decide say she must carry the pikin go hospital she wan know wetin dey cause the cough wetin dey make the pikin find am hard to breath and how she fit help the pikin my question bi wetin fit make pikin cough seriously and find am hard to breath especially for night which kind danger sign dem suppose wash out for when pikin dey cough which things they suppose avoid to help prevent or reduce this course", "answer": "Wetin fit cause this kind serious night cough and struggle to breathe for pikin na conditions like asthma, severe chest infection (pneumonia), or croup wey dey swell the breathway. These sicknesses dey make the air passage narrow, especially for night when cold air or dust dey trigger am, and na wetin dey make the chest make sound.

Danger signs wey you must watch out for na if the pikin chest dey draw inside go deep as e dey breathe, if the lips or tongue turn blue, or if the pikin dey too weak to drink water or breastfeed. To help the pikin, make una avoid firewood or cigarette smoke, dust, cold night breeze, and the use of strong perfumes or insecticides around the house.

Abeg, no use your hand buy anyhow cough syrup for chemist; carry the pikin go hospital immediately make doctor check the chest and give correct treatment.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "5", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "5", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "1", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "5"}

{"question": "One woman notice say anytime wey dem wake up for morning, her husband go begin cough well well. The cough dey start suddenly and e fit take long time before e go stop. As time dey go, she notice say her husband no fit breathe well again. Anytime wey e waka small distance or climb staircase, e go stop make e catch breath because e dey tire quick quick.

One day, after her husband don spend long time dey cough and dey struggle to catch breath, the woman come fear. E begin think say maybe one sickness dey cause all these problems. The next day, she talk to her husband make dem go hospital go see doctor so dat doctor go fit examine am and know wetin dey really happen.

The question be say, wetin fit make person dey cough like this, with constant tiredness and serious difficulty to breathe anytime the cough start? Na only lung sickness or heart sickness fit cause this kind problem? Which kind sickness fit make person struggle to breathe so much or even cause death if dem no get urgent treatment? Wetin be the danger signs of cough and breathing problem wey family members suppose watch out for, wey mean say the person need urgent medical attention?", "answer": "Dis kain cough wey dey start for morning, plus difficulty to breathe wen person waka small and serious tiredness fit be sign of **heart failure** (heart no dey pump blood well) or **COPD/asthma** (lung disease). Heart failure dey cause fluid for lung wey dey make person cough for morning and no fit breathe well wen dem do small work. Lung sickness like COPD or severe asthma fit cause am too, but heart failure dey more dangerous if dem no treat am quick. **Danger signs wey need urgent hospital** na: person no fit talk well or lie flat, lips/fingers dey turn blue, confusion or fainting, breathing very fast (pass 30 per minute), or chest pain. Carry am go hospital **now now** for oxygen, ECG, chest X-ray and blood test (BNP) to know if na heart or lung and start treatment sharp sharp.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "5", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "5", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "1", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "5"}

{"question": "One woman notice say for the past few days, pikin don dey cough without stopping. At first, she think say na ordinary cold wey catch the pikin for chest and say e go clear by itself. But the cough no gree stop. Every night, the pikin dey wake up suddenly because of the cough. Sometimes, e go dey struggle like say e hard am to breathe well.The woman go carry the pikin upright, and she fit hear the chest dey make sound and dey work hard as the pikin dey breathe. Because of this, the pikin no fit sleep well for night.

One day, after one night wey the pikin cough well-well and dey struggle to breathe properly, the woman decide say she must carry the pikin go hospital. She want know wetin dey cause the cough, wetin dey make the pikin find am hard to breathe, and how she fit help the pikin.

My question be: wetin fit make pikin cough seriously and find am hard to breathe, especially for night? Which kind danger signs dem suppose watch out for when pikin dey cough? Which things dem suppose avoid to help prevent or reduce this cough?", "answer": "Dis kind cough wey dey make pikin struggle to breathe, especially at night with "wheezing" sound, fit be **Asthma** or **Severe Pneumonia** because of heavy mucus or lung inflammation. For our area, common causes like dusty environment, smoke, or infections fit trigger dis condition well-well. You must carry the pikin go hospital sharp-sharp because struggle to breathe (respiratory distress) and fast breathing na emergency wey fit kill pikin. Warning signs to watch out for na if the pikin skin dey pull in for chest or neck (recessions), if e dey breathe very fast, or if e no fit feed/drink water. To help, avoid smoke, dust, and heavy perfumes, and make sure the pikin room dey clean and well-ventilated.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "5", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "4", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "1", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "2"}

{"question": "One woman carry him pikin wey dey 3 years come hospital this morning for check up Wetin make dem bring am come be say anytime dem talk to pikin e no dey respondall E no dey answer e no dey look person wey dey talk to am Even if dem call him name e no dey show say e dey hear anything When we ask the mama whether the pikin don ever get seizure before She talk say the pikin never get seizure all We still ask whether the pikin come collect all him immunization vaccine as e suppose We check the medical card wey the mama bring and e show say na true the pikin collect all the immunization vaccine wey e suppose collect complete My next question be say for this kind case where the pikin never get seizure before and e don collect all im immunization vaccine complete Wetin fit make this kind thing happen to the pikin", "answer": "For this kind case, the first major thing wey fit cause am na hearing loss (make the pikin no dey hear), wey fit start from birth, from serious jaundice when dem born am, or from some strong injection like Gentamicin. Another reason fit be ear infection wey don tey or fluid wey block the ear (glue ear) wey dey make sound hard to enter.

If to say the pikin dey hear but e no just dey look person face or answer name, e fit be Autism Spectrum Disorder (ASD) wey dey affect how pikin dey relate with people. Even though the pikin take all vaccines, these ones fit still happen because immunization no dey prevent autism, genetic hearing loss, or hearing damage from other causes.

E good make dem carry the pikin go see ENT doctor make dem test him hearing, and pediatrician to check him brain and behavior development sharp-sharp.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "5", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "5", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "1", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "5"}

{"question": "One woman notice say for the past few days, pikin don dey cough without stopping. At first, she think say na ordinary cold wey catch the pikin for chest and say e go clear by itself. But the cough no gree stop. Every night, the pikin dey wake up suddenly because of the cough. Sometimes, e go dey struggle like say e hard am to breathe well.The woman go carry the pikin upright, and she fit hear the chest dey make sound and dey work hard as the pikin dey breathe. Because of this, the pikin no fit sleep well for night.

One day, after one night wey the pikin cough well-well and dey struggle to breathe properly, the woman decide say she must carry the pikin go hospital. She want know wetin dey cause the cough, wetin dey make the pikin find am hard to breathe, and how she fit help the pikin.

My question be: wetin fit make pikin cough seriously and find am hard to breathe, especially for night? Which kind danger signs dem suppose watch out for when pikin dey cough? Which things dem suppose avoid to help prevent or reduce this cough?", "answer": "Dis one fit be bronchiolitis or asthma wey dey common for pikin dem, especially if e dey worse for night and you dey hear wheezing sound for chest. Danger signs wey you suppose watch well na: fast breathing or chest dey pull in, blue lips or tongue, pikin too weak to suck or drink, high fever wey no gree come down, or if pikin dey sleep too much and hard to wake am. Make you avoid smoke, dust, cold air, and people wey dey cough near the pikin; no give cough syrup or antibiotic unless doctor talk am. Breastfeed well well, use saline drops and suction for nose if e block, and keep pikin head small raise when e dey sleep. Carry am go hospital quick quick if any danger sign show face because e fit need oxygen or nebulizer.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "5", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "5", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "1", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "5"}

{"question": "One woman carry him pikin wey dey 3 years come hospital this morning for check up Wetin make dem bring am come be say anytime dem talk to pikin e no dey respondall E no dey answer e no dey look person wey dey talk to am Even if dem call him name e no dey show say e dey hear anything When we ask the mama whether the pikin don ever get seizure before She talk say the pikin never get seizure all We still ask whether the pikin come collect all him immunization vaccine as e suppose We check the medical card wey the mama bring and e show say na true the pikin collect all the immunization vaccine wey e suppose collect complete My next question be say for this kind case where the pikin never get seizure before and e don collect all im immunization vaccine complete Wetin fit make this kind thing happen to the pikin", "answer": "Based on wetin you describe, the main problem be say the pikin no dey respond when dem call am, no dey look person, no dey answer name. This kind sign na wetin we dey suspect for **Autism Spectrum Disorder (ASD)** or **hearing impairment (deafness)**, and na these two you must first commot for road.

The reason be say the pikin don complete all immunization, so measles or meningitis wey fit cause deafness no too likely, but you still gatz check the ear well well with hearing test. Since e no ever get seizure, condition like epilepsy wey dey affect brain no dey likely too.

My advice na make you do **hearing assessment** first (audiometry or OAE test) to know whether na deafness dey cause am. If the ear dey okay, then you go check for autism sign like whether pikin dey make eye contact, dey play with other children, get repetitive movement, or get delay for talking. Make you refer the pikin go see specialist (paediatrician or ENT) for proper evaluation and early intervention, because early help dey improve outcome well well.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "5", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "5", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "1", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "5"}

{"question": "One mama wey dey always bring her pikin come for injection talk say she don notice say her newborn baby get problem for mouth area, and the baby lips dey look blue.

Today too, she notice say anytime she dey breastfeed the baby, the baby dey struggle, dey gasp for air, and e dey find am hard to breathe well. She say na this one make her worry because she no know wetin dey happen to the baby.

Wetin fit make newborn baby lips dey look blue? Wetin fit make baby dey struggle and find am hard to breathe anytime e dey suck breast? Medicine fit solve the problem, abi the baby need make doctor examine am first?", "answer": "Mama, abeg carry di pikin go hospital sharp-sharp because dis matter na emergency. Di pikin mouth problem and di blue skin (cyanosis) mean say di baby no dey get enough oxygen, wey fit be because di mouth problem dey block way di baby dey breathe. Di struggle and gasping show say di pikin dey struggle to take air, and dis fit cause heart or lung problem if we no treat am now. No try use any breast medicine or soap, because dem no go fit cure dis physical block for di pikin mouth. You must see doctor now to clear di mouth and make sure di pikin fit breathe well again.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "5", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "5", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "1", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "5"}

{"question": "One woman dem carry come hospital this morning because she dey bleed plenty, and the bleeding don make her weak well-well. Dem ask am whether this kind thing don happen before, and she talk say e don happen about two times before. Anytime e happen, she dey feel pain and the bleeding dey come and stop, then come start again.

Dem come ask am whether e fit be say belle dey comot, but she talk say she no know whether she get belle or not. Dem ask am when she last see her monthly period, and she talk say not too long, say na about one month and two weeks ago she last see her period before this heavy bleeding start again this morning.

Abeg, wetin fit make dis woman bleed this kind plenty? Wetin be the emergency things wey health workers suppose do immediately? Wetin be the treatment wey fit save her life and stop the bleeding? Which medicine or injection wey fit help control the bleeding fit be given first? And which tests or investigations fit be done to know the real cause of this serious bleeding?", "answer": "I no fit give you medicine, because I no see the woman, but the symptoms suggest the woman may have a problem with her uterus or ovaries. She needs an ultrasound scan and tests to check the size and position of her uterus, as well as for any abnormal growth. This will help to know the root cause of the heavy bleeding and recurring cramps. The doctor will then decide on the best treatment, which could involve medication or surgery. The priority is to stop the bleeding and address the underlying issue as soon as possible.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "5", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "4", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "1", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "5"}

{"question": "One woman wey dey live for her house she dey work she dey do her work well well and she no get any health wahala One day as she been dey baff she been touch her breast and she con see say one kind small thing wey strong dey like ball bin dey inside that 1st time she been She been feel say no be something wey serious but she come touch am again another day con see say e still dey for there As time come pass she come de fear She begin to worry about whether the matter bin dey develop for inside her breast E been no dey pain am but the fact say the something been strong and And e been no dey gree go been make she come sad She con also start to dey remember some tori wey she been dey hear about girls wey dey get this kind strong thing for their breast After some weeks pass she decide to go see dr She been wan know wetin cause the strong thing and wetin wey she need do to make sure say her health go remain calm way My questions be say wetin fit cause this kind strong thing for inside woman breast Na every strong thing wey dey for breast na im mean say e go come lead to cancer Which other things for breast dey wey women suppose de check out", "answer": "**Wetin fit cause am:** Plenty things fit cause strong lump for breast, and no be all of dem na cancer. Common ones na **fibroadenoma** (dis one common for young women, e dey smooth, e dey move well-well, e no dey pain), **breast cyst** (water dey inside am), **fibrocystic change** (wey dey come and go with monthly period), and infection or **abscess**. Some lump fit be **cancer** too, especially if e strong well-well, e no dey move, e get rough edge, or skin/nipple change dey.

**Na every lump be cancer?** No o! Plenty breast lump na benign (dem no dangerous), and fibroadenoma na di most common for women wey never old reach.

**Odder things wey woman suppose check:** She suppose watch out for **lump wey no dey move, change for breast size or shape, nipple wey turn inside or dey release blood/fluid, skin wey dey pull or look like orange peel, and swelling for armpit.** My advice na make she go hospital make dem do **examination, ultrasound scan** (or mammogram if she don old), and if e necessary **biopsy** to know exactly wetin di lump be — early check dey save life.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "5", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "5", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "1", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "5"}

{"question": "One woman notice say for the past few days, pikin don dey cough without stopping. At first, she think say na ordinary cold wey catch the pikin for chest and say e go clear by itself. But the cough no gree stop. Every night, the pikin dey wake up suddenly because of the cough. Sometimes, e go dey struggle like say e hard am to breathe well.The woman go carry the pikin upright, and she fit hear the chest dey make sound and dey work hard as the pikin dey breathe. Because of this, the pikin no fit sleep well for night.

One day, after one night wey the pikin cough well-well and dey struggle to breathe properly, the woman decide say she must carry the pikin go hospital. She want know wetin dey cause the cough, wetin dey make the pikin find am hard to breathe, and how she fit help the pikin.

My question be: wetin fit make pikin cough seriously and find am hard to breathe, especially for night? Which kind danger signs dem suppose watch out for when pikin dey cough? Which things dem suppose avoid to help prevent or reduce this cough?", "answer": "Pikin na likely na case of bronchiolitis or pneumonia. Wetin fit make pikin cough serious na bacteria or virus, like RSV or influenza. Danger sign wey fit watch out for include fever, wheezing, and rapid breathing. Woman should avoid smoke, dust, and strong smells. She fit give pikin fluids and monitor temperature. If pikin no fit breathe well, she fit take him to hospital for oxygen and antibiotics.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "5", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "2", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "3", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "4"}

{"question": "This morning one woman wey born for our place deliver her pikin early for Dune Around 8 00 am di person wey dey with am for her call us say the woman dey shiver Her body hot well well and she dey complain of plenty body pain We She check di home cover am with cloth and check her temperature Her temperature na 38 2 We come do malaria rapid test for am and e show say di woman get malaria We ask am whether she don chop and she say she never chop any anything We tell di people wey dey with am make dem give am tea wey she drink We ask whether she don breastfeed di baby She say as she wan breastfeed di baby she notice say di baby don stool We help di woman sit up and lean back for di bed so her body fit feel small better We check am again and see say her eyes no pale We advise say as soon as she don chop make she take paracetamol After she take the paracetamol we con decide when next she fit take another dose Since the malaria test confirm say she get malaria we fit continue with the append ate treatment Because she still dey feel weak If she no improve after eating and taking paracetamol we fit know the next treatment wey go fit am", "answer": "**Wetin you don do so far good well well, but make we add some important things:**

Since di woman just born pikin (postpartum) and she get fever with malaria, you must quick start correct antimalarial treatment — for breastfeeding mama, ACT like Artemether-Lumefantrine (Coartem) dey safe, so start am sharp sharp after she chop, no delay am. But you must know say fever after delivery no be malaria alone — you gats check for postpartum sepsis or womb infection (puerperal sepsis), so check her lochia (di blood wey dey comot), press her belle to feel di womb, and smell whether di discharge get bad odour. Encourage her make she continue breastfeed di pikin — di stooling na normal newborn passing meconium, e no be bad thing.

**My strong advice: dis kind fever for new mama fit turn serious quick, so if di temperature no come down, or she get bad-smelling discharge, plenty bleeding, or she just dey weak pass, make you refer am go bigger hospital sharp sharp for proper checkup and IV treatment.** No wait too long, because postpartum infection fit kill fast.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "5", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "5", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "1", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "5"}

{"question": "One woman notice say anytime wey dem wake up for morning, her husband go begin cough well well. The cough dey start suddenly and e fit take long time before e go stop. As time dey go, she notice say her husband no fit breathe well again. Anytime wey e waka small distance or climb staircase, e go stop make e catch breath because e dey tire quick quick.

