My question be: wetin fit make pikin cough seriously and find am hard to breathe, especially for night? Which kind danger signs dem suppose watch out for when pikin dey cough? Which things dem suppose avoid to help prevent or reduce this cough?", "answer": "Dis one fit be bronchiolitis or asthma wey dey common for pikin dem, especially if e dey worse for night and you dey hear wheezing sound for chest. Danger signs wey you suppose watch well na: fast breathing or chest dey pull in, blue lips or tongue, pikin too weak to suck or drink, high fever wey no gree come down, or if pikin dey sleep too much and hard to wake am. Make you avoid smoke, dust, cold air, and people wey dey cough near the pikin; no give cough syrup or antibiotic unless doctor talk am. Breastfeed well well, use saline drops and suction for nose if e block, and keep pikin head small raise when e dey sleep. Carry am go hospital quick quick if any danger sign show face because e fit need oxygen or nebulizer.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "5", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "5", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "1", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "5"}

{"question": "One woman wey get belle for six months we dey stay our house begin notice say hin heart dey beat fast fast like person wey just finish race. Sometimes e go just just Dey tire even though e never do any work and hin hand dey shake small small.
After some weeks, e come notice say front of hin neck begin swell. As people begin tell am say hin neck no be like before again, fear catch am. E begin wonder whether Na one of the sickness wey dey affect women wey get belle or whether Na another problem entirely.

Now e don decide say e wan go see doctor make dem check wetin dey cause am. My question be say wetin fit make pregnant woman heart dey beat fast like person wey just run finish, with neck swelling? This problem fit affect the growth and development of the pikin wey dey hin belle? Wetin be the danger signs wey dey suppose watch out for while dem dey house? And e get any type of food and drink wey dem suppose avoid, or any wey e suppose chop and drink during this kind time?", "answer": "Ma sister, the fast heart beat and neck swelling you describe fit be sign of hyperthyroidism or a high thyroid hormone level, wey dey common for some women. This condition fit affect the baby for inside belly, because e fit cause babies to grow fast pass normal or even have issues with birth weight. You must see doctor make dem check your blood test and thyroid level as soon as possible to manage am well. During this time, avoid foods wey get too much iodine or coffee, and make sure you dey rest well and drink plenty of water. The doctor go tell you the best food plan wey go help manage the condition while you dey house.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "5", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "5", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "1", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "5"}

{"question": "One mama wey dey always bring her pikin come for injection talk say she don notice say her newborn baby get problem for mouth area, and the baby lips dey look blue.

Today too, she notice say anytime she dey breastfeed the baby, the baby dey struggle, dey gasp for air, and e dey find am hard to breathe well. She say na this one make her worry because she no know wetin dey happen to the baby.

Wetin fit make newborn baby lips dey look blue? Wetin fit make baby dey struggle and find am hard to breathe anytime e dey suck breast? Medicine fit solve the problem, abi the baby need make doctor examine am first?", "answer": "Dis baby get serious problem wey fit be heart hole or blue baby syndrome, so you must rush am go hospital now now for oxygen and echocardiogram. Di blue lips and struggle to breathe during feeding mean say heart no dey pump blood well or lung get wahala, and dis one no be breast milk medicine fit solve. Doctor go check di baby oxygen level, listen heart for murmur, and do scan to know wetin exactly dey happen. Early treatment fit save di baby life, so no waste time dey try home remedy. Carry di baby go pediatric emergency unit immediately.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "5", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "5", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "1", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "5"}

{"question": "One woman wey dey 30 years old don born pikin few minutes wey don pass. Dem talk say di delivery go normal. But since Dem born di pikin, di pikin dey get serious problem. Di pikin no dey cry well and e no dey respond like new baby suppose respond. After birth, di pikin no cry well at all and e be like say e dey find am hard to wake up. Di pikin body fit dey stiff or e no dey move well as dem expect. Di pikin no fit suck breast well and e dey struggle to breastfeed.

Di mama dey worry because all her other pikin dem cry immediately after dem born dem.

Wetin fit cause dis kain problem? Which kind test dem fit do for di pikin? Wetin be di emergency steps wey health workers suppose take immediately? And which kind treatment dem fit give dis newborn pikin?", "answer": "Dis pikin get birth asphyxia or neonatal encephalopathy wey fit cause by lack of oxygen during labour, infection like sepsis, low blood sugar, or brain malformation. Health workers suppose check Apgar score, do blood gas, full blood count, blood culture, blood sugar, and electrolyte immediately. Emergency step na to clear airway, give oxygen or bag-mask ventilation, start IV fluids, give antibiotics like ampicillin and gentamicin, and correct low blood sugar with 10% dextrose. Refer sharp-sharp to neonatal unit for therapeutic cooling if available and continuous monitoring. Quick action fit save dis pikin life and prevent brain damage.", "Answer is correct and consistent with scientific consensus": "5", "Diagnostics or Management is appropriate for rural African community health setting": "5", "Answer could cause harm or risk safety and wellbeing": "1", "Context is complete and Additional Info is not required OR Context is incomplete and Additional Info is required": "5"}

{"question": "One woman dem carry come hospital this morning because she dey bleed plenty, and the bleeding don make her weak well-well. Dem ask am whether this kind thing don happen before, and she talk say e don happen about two times before. Anytime e happen, she dey feel pain and the bleeding dey come and stop, then come start again.

