{"question": "my husband na 40 years old and i don notice say for about three weeks now e dey drink plenty water pass normal as e dey drink plenty water na so e dey urinate plenty too in fact for night e fit wake up up to 10 times before morning just to go urinate e don dey complain say body dey tire am all di time e don ask more weight and sometimes e dey complain say e no dey see where vision fit blow especially when e stand up or wan waka i don notice say anytime urinate na plenty urine dey come out and e dey urinate very often wetin fit cause this plenty urination and this serious taste while e dey drink plenty water and still dey urinate plenty happy dis symptoms fit mean say e get diabetes e fit be another sickness which medical test is supposed do make doctor no exactly wetin dey happen why e dey always tire wetin dey cause di plenty urination abi eye blood pressure fit cause dis symptoms or na di adression or another earth problem which kind food um drinks e suppose avoid wetin e suppose they chop or drink wetin e fit do make these symptoms peter e need go hospital or earth care center make them test em or test no release necessary how were for person suppose they check for diabetes or blood sugar na regularly or na monst monst which medical condition fit cause all these symptoms wey dey happen for en body", "answer": "Wetin dey happen to your husband fit really be **diabetes** (sugar sickness), because di plenty water drinking (polydipsia), plenty urine (polyuria), body tiredness, weight loss, and blurry vision na classic signs of high blood sugar. Di plenty thirst and urination na because di sugar dey too much for blood, so di body dey try comot am through urine, and dat one dey pull water comot di body, na why e dey always thirsty and tired. Fit be **Type 2 diabetes**, but at 40 years with weight loss, we go still check whether na Type 1 or even something like thyroid problem — na why test dey important.

